====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|UK}} A stone, block of wood, or anything else, placed under a wheel or barrel to prevent motion; a scotch; a skid.
#*{{quote-book|en|year=1850|author=w:Sylvester Judd|title=Richard Edney and the Governor's Family|passage=You might as well smite that saw with your fist ; you might as well put a '''trig''' under the dam and stop it, as to practise on him}}
# The [[mark]] for [[player]]s at [[skittles]], etc.

====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To stop (a wheel, barrel, etc.) by placing something under it; to [[scotch]]; to [[skid]].

